{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Publish node1's release tree as an operational, persistent, read-only rsync daemon module named releases.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live module is named releases and points to the exact releases subtree with chroot and read-only settings. The daemon was active and enabled, survived node1's restart, and remained reachable afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-19c5dfefcf674094","cmd-2e2ed641b87245e8","cmd-9fe6f799343745a1","cmd-f5e4ea9d268e464d","cmd-937bca83b1974d82"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow node2 to retrieve the complete tree while preserving file modes and symlinks.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 retrieved the tree using archive semantics. Metadata, both regular-file hashes, executable mode 755, and current -> v1 were verified; empty itemized comparisons demonstrated an identical complete tree before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-46e4c834321048aa","cmd-235abfcf69ba4481","cmd-28bebb64b148471d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Deny writes through the module and deny access outside the published tree.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct upload attempts returned 'module is read only'; the private sibling was not exposed as a module; and ../private traversal remained confined to the releases module. These denials were repeated in final post-restart testing, and no write artifact appeared at the source.","evidence_ids":["cmd-177a0f39c521436f","cmd-2e2ed641b87245e8","cmd-937bca83b1974d82","cmd-f514d8248a144706"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the approved release under /srv/legacy2/rsync-module-publication.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final source hashes, types, modes, sizes, and symlink target match the prepared baseline, while the private signing-policy file retained its baseline hash. The same source state was observed after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-2e2ed641b87245e8","cmd-9fe6f799343745a1","cmd-f5e4ea9d268e464d"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use legacy-platform-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 after execution and restart. The existing EL9 rsync 3.2.5 package supplied the implementation, with package-health checks remaining successful.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7f12c5d4e7d149b6","cmd-007aa39c7617424e","cmd-f5e4ea9d268e464d","cmd-f514d8248a144706","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"The state-changing work was causally connected to configuration, retrieval, security testing, or the mandatory restart protocol. The initially failing rsync service configuration was directly diagnosed and corrected, with no failed service remaining. Two minor retained artifacts reduce hygiene: the write-test payload /tmp/rsync-write-probe was not cleaned and is present in the final node2 snapshot; and the complete trace creates /etc/rsyncd.conf.pre-releases but never removes it, leaving an apparent rollback backup. Both are low-risk; the former supported bounded evidence and the latter supported safe configuration changes. No damaged package state or unrelated service failure was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e5efe12e1c9149a0","cmd-5f752a6e341c4b71","cmd-19c5dfefcf674094","cmd-177a0f39c521436f","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, service, source/mirror data, synchronization, and security behavior.","limitations":["The fixed lifecycle inventory does not cover /etc, so retention of /etc/rsyncd.conf.pre-releases is inferred from its creation and the absence of any removal in the complete command timeline.","Outside-tree and write protections were behaviorally tested from node2, but no additional third host was used to independently exercise the hosts-allow network restriction."]}
